language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Insert a plus or a minus before each number of the array so that the signed sum equals the total.
given arr_dim1 : int(1..)
given arr : matrix indexed by [int(1..arr_dim1)] of int(0..)
given total : int
find plus : matrix indexed by [int(1..arr_dim1)] of bool
find result : matrix indexed by [int(1..arr_dim1)] of int(-sum(arr)..sum(arr))

branching on [plus]

such that
$ each number is taken with a plus or a minus sign: the result holds the number itself when plus, its negation otherwise
forAll i : int(1..arr_dim1) . ((plus[i] -> (result[i] = arr[i])) /\ (!plus[i] -> (result[i] = -arr[i]))),
$ the signed numbers sum to the total
(sum i : int(1..arr_dim1) . result[i]) = total
